Compute $f(-x)$:
\begin{align*}
f(-x) &= \log \left( -x + \sqrt[3]{1 + (-x)^3} \right) \\
&= \log \left( -x + \sqrt[3]{1 + x^3} \right).
\end{align*}
We need to compare $f(-x)$ with $f(x)$ and $-f(x)$:
\begin{align*}
f(x) &= \log \left( x + \sqrt[3]{1 + x^3} \right), \\
-f(x) &= -\log \left( x + \sqrt[3]{1 + x^3} \right).
\end{align*}
Since neither:
\begin{align*}
-x + \sqrt[3]{1 + x^3} &\neq x + \sqrt[3]{1 + x^3}, \\
-x + \sqrt[3]{1 + x^3} &\neq - \left( x + \sqrt[3]{1 + x^3} \right),
\end{align*}
we conclude that replacing $x$ with $-x$ in the function does not result in the function or its negative. Thus, $f(x)$ is neither even nor odd, and we have $\boxed{\text{neither}}$.

